    "summary": "The Puntland House of Representatives' Social Affairs Committee conducted an oversight visit to the Ministry of Education today, reviewing its performance and programs.",
    "content": "The Social Affairs, Culture, Information and Communication Committee of the Puntland House of Representatives visited the Ministry of Education today to evaluate the ministry's performance and ongoing initiatives. The delegation was led by the committee chair, alongside other members, and they held a working meeting with senior ministry officials.\n\nDuring the visit, the committee reviewed the ministry's achievements in the recent period, including curriculum development and teacher training programs. The inspection aimed to identify gaps and ensure the ministry aligns with legislative oversight requirements.\n\nThis oversight activity is part of the parliament's constitutional mandate to monitor the executive branch. The committee plans to continue such visits to other government institutions in the coming weeks.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this report signals the importance of transparency in Puntland's education sector, which directly affects youth development and community investment. Diaspora contributions to education in Puntland can be better tracked when institutions are scrutinized.\n\nThe committee commended the ministry's efforts but noted areas needing improvement, particularly in resource allocation and school infrastructure. They pledged to share detailed findings in a formal report.\n\nRead the original report from Horseed Media here: https://horseedmedia.net/guddiga-arrimaha-bulshada-ee-golaha-wakiillada-puntland-oo-kormeer-shaqo-ku-sameeyey-wasaaradda-waxbarashada/424176/",
